    "rating": 3.7,
    "reference": "ChIJewX00-s3yUwRlkzhPaotNMg",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Noah Sampaio",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102520037641072919876/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocL6MbOEfQQN4yFkDzks97oukOKt-NO1S6eK78NqFUSMgynL0g=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "2 months ago",
        "text": "It’s actually insane how high the prices are. For used clothing, you pay the same as (sometimes MORE than) regular pricing. Some of the prices went up 5 times since 2 years ago. A CD used to be 1.99 plus tax and now they’re at least 4.99 plus tax. A small bundle of yarn that would cost at most 5 dollars at walmart (for the exact same brand mind you) is 5.99 plus tax here. Are you serious?",
        "time": 1764202786,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "L L",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101371609862706276121/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVOC-4lDPf6pm-jnEATH8poVLXYWcAIkSQEaeG4TujtBGjj0Yoe=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 2,
        "relative_time_description": "3 months ago",
        "text": "I found some books there that are priced at 6.99+tax that can be found at Nova for $2 with no tax. There are items that are ridiculously expensive given that they are donated and not in great shape. What warrants the ongoing price gouging when there are no fitting rooms, no refunds and there is one employee manning the self check out?",
        "time": 1763302999,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "J T",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103988878020531278923/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJBI7v3bFTi3n-XzpScCIBAsE5CdwljLJkH54lZykPXP83R4As=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4",
        "rating": 4,
        "relative_time_description": "5 months ago",
        "text": "Nice and spacious. Clean as well. However I haven’t found anything good every time I go. Maybe it’s just the area.",
        "time": 1758085932,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Bryanna Clarke",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100351872444214624321/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUBWbq5PQJigNhwzcIX4RBVCeVKAyBM1cbCoAMktGXNLrUUwK5qMg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "10 months ago",
        "text": "Worst customer service I’ve experienced in a long time. One of the associates refused to speak English. I also work with the public and speak fluent French. It is a courtesy to the customer to communicate in their language. Both her and the supervisor were adamant to pay the difference on an article of clothing I wanted to exchange due to a defect. Perhaps better inspection before putting on the rack? I had used a coupon on the original purchase. The exchange was a similar article of clothing with an identical price; however they insisted they could not honour the same price after the small discount applied on my original purchase. We are talking pennies here, but it is the principle on how the situation was dealt with. Value Village, our family enjoyed stopping in monthly and graciously giving our donations; however, there are many other local thrift stores with 10x better customer service and who speak to me in my language. Do better.",
        "time": 1743275045,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Evelina Gevorkyan",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100796703910208851602/reviews",
